<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Mongera et al. (2018) & Kim et al. (2021) zebrafish tailbud active fluid-to-solid jamming transition & yield-stress axis elongation — Code-to-model traceability: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring (L1-94) maps every Pass 2 and Pass 3 step to its source figure/equation and to the 6 Lean theorems; each new function docstring states its equation, its source and the Lean theorem it instantiates (L398-514, L521-640), and the math-KG YAML registers the two new laws with code and Lean loci. Deductions: the clock advection floor 0.15/0.85 and the slowing exponent (L576-583), the sheath taper constants 95/35 um (L398-406) and the f_FN sigmoid 110/40 um (L409-429) are stated but not traced to a figure (-5); the hard-coded asymmetry overrides at L724-728 still carry no citation (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Mongera et al. (2018) & Kim et al. (2021) zebrafish tailbud active fluid-to-solid jamming transition & yield-stress axis elongation — Model fidelity to source: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The Mongera/Kim laws of Pass 2 are unchanged and remain faithful: cell packing, Maxwell coordination, rigidity-percolation yield stress, Kramers T1 rate, Bingham strain rate and the continuous AP crossover solver (L194-390). Pass 3 adds the requested fibronectin and clock couplings as reduced models that are honest about their status: a hoop-equilibrium sheath with an explicit calibration note (L398-514; reference JSON L269-286) and a phase-advection clock with a mechanical arrest gate (L521-640), both wired bidirectionally into the jamming gradient (arrest front -> somite fibronectin -> channeling -> v_elong -> somite length) and backed by Lean Theorems 5-6. Deductions: the remediation asked for ECM boundary FRICTION, and the implemented coupling is confinement — the computed wall-friction force (L485-486) is reported but never feeds back (-3); the channeling factor is a transient stored-volume argument rather than a steady-state force balance, and it multiplies an elongation law that is still a calibrated product (J prefactor 2.034, tanh(sigma_A/29) fluidity, blebbistatin/SU5402 asymmetry overrides at L716-728) (-4); Lambda_arrest = 4, the u(x) floor 0.15 and c_slow = 0.6 (L576-583) are modelling choices without a cited measurement, and the clock is a phase model, not the Lewis (2003) DDE (-3). Down 3 from v2 because the new modules make the phenomenological core more visible, not less." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2022-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming.py L683–L728: 2D simulator: sheath channeling multiplies the elongation law; J prefactor, tanh fluidity and hard-coded blebbistatin/SU5402 asymmetry overrides remain phenomenological <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2022-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming.py#L683-L728>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Mongera et al. (2018) & Kim et al. (2021) zebrafish tailbud active fluid-to-solid jamming transition & yield-stress axis elongation — Morphometric validation: 89/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1734-1862) now returns 14 measurements with units and references: the 8 Pass 2 metrics (MPZ/A-PSM yield stress, 7-point sigma_y and k_T1 correlations, WT-cdh2 speed drop, cdh2 asymmetry, N = 391 nuclei, specimen compaction r = 0.9915) plus 6 Pass 3 metrics (fn1a;fn1b speed ratio 0.79 vs ~0.70, width ratio 1.24 vs ~1.20, arrest front 161 vs ~180 um, Cooke-Zeeman S 46.2 vs ~47 um, frozen stripe wavelength vs S, cdh2 peak jamming ratio vs the gate). Deductions: the Dray ratios, the 47 um somite length, the 180 um arrest front and the 0.45 um/min PSM shortening are approximate anchors flagged as such (reference JSON L288-333), not digitised figure values with uncertainties (-5); the stripe-wavelength-vs-S check is a numerical consistency test of the advection scheme (both derive from v_front), not a biological validation (-3); the itga5 regime misses its approximate ratio by 16% (0.95 vs 0.82) and this is only reported via the 3-regime RMSE (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "datasets/neuromesodermal_jamming/neuromesodermal_jamming_reference.json L288–L333: Dray-2013 ratios and clock anchors are explicitly approximate (approximate_digitization: true, uncertainty_pct 25) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/datasets/neuromesodermal_jamming/neuromesodermal_jamming_reference.json#L288-L333>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-measurement-ap-t1-rearrangement-rate-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-measurement-ap-yield-stress-profile-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-measurement-cdh2-knockdown-lr-asymmetry-pct>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-measurement-cdh2-morphant-peak-jamming-ratio>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-measurement-fn1a-fn1b-morphant-elongation-speed-ratio>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-measurement-fn1a-fn1b-morphant-tailbud-width-ratio>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-measurement-specimen-ap-ecs-compaction-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-measurement-specimen-segmented-nuclei-count>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-measurement-wt-apsm-yield-stress-pa>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-measurement-wt-clock-arrest-front-um>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-measurement-wt-cooke-zeeman-somite-length-um>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-measurement-wt-frozen-her1-stripe-wavelength-um>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-measurement-wt-mpz-yield-stress-pa>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-measurement-wt-vs-cdh2-elongation-speed-drop-um-per-min>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-overall> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Mongera et al. (2018) & Kim et al. (2021) zebrafish tailbud active fluid-to-solid jamming transition & yield-stress axis elongation — MorphoEval overall 90.0/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `2022-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming.py` (90.0/100, down 1.4 from 91.4 in Pass 2). The one open v2 item is closed in a reduced, explicitly labelled form: a quasi-3D fibronectin sheath (`compute_sheath_channeling`, L452-499) couples Dray et al. (2013) cell-fibronectin loss to tailbud widening and slower elongation through a hoop-equilibrium channeling factor (fn1a;fn1b MO v/v_WT = 0.79 vs ~0.70, width 1.24 vs ~1.20), and a Her1/Her7 clock advection solver (`solve_segmentation_clock_arrest`, L546-640) arrests the clock at a jamming-ratio gate strictly anterior to the fluid-to-solid crossover (161 vs 81 um) and yields Cooke-Zeeman somites of 46.2 um (ref ~47 um; frozen stripe wavelength 46.2 um), with somite fibronectin feeding back into the sheath. Six Lean 4 theorems (2 new), 14 measurements (6 new), 13 self-test checks and 9 DOIs back the script. The score drops slightly because the new modules multiply a still-phenomenological elongation law (prefactor, tanh fluidity, hard-coded asymmetry overrides at L716-728), the new reference values are approximate digitisations, the arrest gate and several clock constants are uncited modelling choices, and row C carries no specimen. Overall 90.0/100 (faithfulness 89.2, reproducibility 92.0); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 88, Parameter expressivity 91, Morphometric validation 89, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/neuromesodermal_jamming_comparison.png: rendered output of 2022-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming.py at d58a084, image/png, 1060623 B, 3150×2010 px, artifact_sha256 57d7a446903c3cc022726dc33c7904454b93ad9f642da0182f250a8fb9e200a3 (sha256 57d7a446903c3cc022726dc33c7904454b93ad9f642da0182f250a8fb9e200a3), spec_fingerprint 5225f2c29acda8d1ee81d082219556f85a1159006d552c629f56ce7d8a842027. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 5225f2c29acda8d1ee81d082219556f85a1159006d552c629f56ce7d8a842027; artifact_sha256: 57d7a446903c3cc022726dc33c7904454b93ad9f642da0182f250a8fb9e200a3. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-neuromesodermal-jamming-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Mongera et al. (2018) Nature 561:401-405 Figs. 1-4: along the posterior-to-anterior axis of the zebrafish tailbud, extracellular space fraction phi_ECS(x) decreases from ~14.5% in the posterior Mesodermal Progenitor Zone (MPZ) to ~4.9% in the Anterior Presomitic Mesoderm (A-PSM), driving cell packing phi_pack = 1 - phi_ECS across the rigidity-percolation threshold phi_c approx 0.860 and elevating ferrofluid-measured yield stress sigma_y(x) from ~11 Pa to ~118 Pa while active Myosin-II tension fluctuations sigma_A(x) decline from ~50 Pa to ~13 Pa. | Kim et al. (2021) Nature Physics 17:859-866 & Mongera et al. (2018) Fig. 4: active tension fluctuations fluidize the MPZ (sigma_A > sigma_y) via frequent T1 neighbor exchanges, whereas the jammed solid A-PSM (sigma_y >> sigma_A) serves as an internal mechanical backstop that rectifies MPZ progenitor addition into unidirectional posterior elongation and preserves left-right symmetry; N-cadherin (cdh2) knockdown expands phi_ECS > 14%, unjamming the PSM, slowing elongation, and inducing bilateral body-axis asymmetry. | Dray et al. (2013) Current Biology 23:1335-1341 Figs. 1-4: a fibronectin matrix wraps the tailbud and PSM; fn1a;fn1b double morphants and itga5 morphants lose this boundary, elongate the trunk more slowly and show altered posterior tissue shape and mechanics (the script vendors these as APPROXIMATE ratios, v/v_WT ~0.70 / ~0.82, width ~1.20 / ~1.08, +/-25%). | Herrgen et al. (2010) / Soroldoni et al. (2014): the zebrafish her1/her7 clock period is ~23.5 min at 28 C and clock waves slow and compress toward the anterior PSM before arresting into somite stripes (Cooke-Zeeman S = v_front T).; reconstructed_in_script: Continuous posterior-to-anterior active-foam & Bingham viscoplastic solver across x in [0, 300] um (`solve_ap_jamming_profile`, r_sigma_y = 0.9989, r_kT1 = 0.9922, jamming crossover x* = 81.0 um) and 2D U-shaped tailbud cellular flow simulator across 5 experimental regimes (WT Control, cdh2 Morphant, Blebbistatin, SU5402, Zero-Backstop Ablation; v_elong r = 0.9748, L-R asymmetry r = 0.9851). | (Pass 3) Quasi-3D fibronectin sheath: f_FN(x) profile, hoop equilibrium eps_r = max(0, sigma_A - sigma_y)/(K_FN f_FN + K_t), equilibrium radius R_eq(x), influx-weighted channeling chi (0.951 WT, 0.907 itga5 MO, 0.736 fn1a;fn1b MO) multiplying the elongation speed, tailbud width ratio (1.04 / 1.08 / 1.24), 12-point fn_scale sweep (monotonic), and a diagnostic wall-friction force F_drag. | (Pass 3) Her1/Her7 clock phase advection in the tip frame with a mechanical arrest gate sigma_y/sigma_A >= 4 (x_arrest = 161.1 um > x_jam = 81.0 um), Cooke-Zeeman somite length S = (v_elong + 0.45) * 23.5 min = 46.2 um, frozen her1 stripe wavelength 46.2 um measured on the kymograph, per-regime arrest fronts (cdh2 and ablation: none), and somite-border fibronectin feedback into the sheath profile. | Nuclear-seeded Voronoi tessellation and regional interstitial space segmentation of the Danio rerio posterior tailbud lightsheet micrograph (`zebrafish_tailbud_psm_specimen.jpg`, IDR0051, N = 391 nuclei, <z> = 5.88, AP compaction r = 0.9915).; transfer_boundary: 2D dorsal-ventral optical-plane projection of the 3D U-shaped zebrafish posterior tailbud and paraxial presomitic mesoderm; the fibronectin sheath is a thin-rod axisymmetric reduction (one radius per AP position), not a 3D boundary mesh. | The sheath channeling argument (influx stored in radial dilation is lost to elongation) is a transient-window argument, not a steady-state Stokes balance; K_FN and K_t are calibrated to the approximate Dray et al. (2013) ratios; the dynamic ECM friction F_drag does not feed back on v_elong. | The clock is a phase oscillator with a prescribed frequency profile and a mechanical arrest gate (Lambda_arrest = 4, a modelling choice standing in for the FGF/Wnt determination front and Yap mechanosensitivity), not the Lewis (2003) her1/her7 delay-differential oscillator; v_PSM-shortening = 0.45 um/min and the ~47 um somite length are approximate anchors.; does_not_claim: Does not model 3D notochord vacuolation turgor mechanics, anterior somite epithelialization clefting, an FGF8/Wnt morphogen determination front, Delta-Notch phase coupling, or a full axisymmetric/3D Stokes-Bingham solve with fibronectin traction boundary conditions.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2022-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming.py:146-147 with datasets/neuromesodermal_jamming/ neuromesodermal_jamming_reference.json:269-315 — K_FN = 2800 Pa and K_t = 40 Pa are calibrated to approximate Dray et al. (2013) ratios (fn1a;fn1b 0.70, itga5 0.82, widths 1.20/1.08) and the itga5 regime misses by 16% (0.95 vs 0.82). Digitise the actual Dray 2013 Fig. 2/4 elongation-rate and tissue-width values with panel pins and uncertainties, and anchor the sheath modulus to a measured ECM/tissue stiffness.",
        "remediation needed: 2022-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming.py:1478-1601 — row C has no vendored specimen: vendor a CC-licensed fibronectin immunostain of the zebrafish tailbud (Dray/Lawton or IDR) and a her1 in situ or Soroldoni (2014) wave image, segment the FN boundary / stripe spacing, and add them as specimen comparisons and measurements (also render the fn1a;fn1b 2D regime, simulated at L1142-1153, as a spatial panel).",
        "remediation needed: 2022-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming.py:452-499 and 485-486 — `compute_sheath_channeling` converts influx stored in radial dilation into a channeling factor (a transient-window argument) and the dynamic cell-ECM wall friction F_drag is computed but never fed back on v_elong, so the v2 request for ECM boundary FRICTION is only half met. Replace with an axisymmetric thin-film Stokes/Bingham solve with a fibronectin traction boundary condition (zeta_FN f_FN v_rel) so friction and confinement both enter the axial force balance.",
        "remediation needed: 2022-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming.py:521-543 and 156 — the clock arrest gate Lambda_arrest = 4 is an uncited modelling choice; the biological determination front is set by FGF8/Wnt (Dubrulle et al. 2001; cf. 2003-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis.py in this repository). Couple x_arrest to an FGF8 gradient threshold and compare the resulting position with her1 in situ / Soroldoni (2014) wave data instead of the P-PSM/A-PSM boundary proxy (ref 180 um).",
        "remediation needed: 2022-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming.py:546-640 — the clock is a phase oscillator with a prescribed omega(x) (floor 0.15/0.85 at L576, c_slow = 0.6 at L159), and the frozen-stripe wavelength check (L615-623, measurement `wt_frozen_her1_stripe_wavelength_um`) is numerically circular with S. Replace the phase model with the Lewis (2003) her1/her7 DDE (or the repository's 2003-lewis script) coupled through the same advection, and validate stripe spacing against measured somite lengths per stage.",
        "remediation needed: 2022-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming.py:716-728 — the elongation law remains a calibrated product (J prefactor 2.034 x backstop x tanh(sigma_A/29) fluidity x chi, ablation special-case 0.41) and the blebbistatin (2.25%) and SU5402 (2.65%) L-R asymmetries are hard-coded overrides; the 5-regime r = 0.9748 therefore partly scores fitted constants. Derive v_elong and the asymmetry from the 2D simulator's own kinematics (tip displacement, left/right length difference) and remove the overrides." ;
    pk1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-parameter-expressivity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Mongera et al. (2018) & Kim et al. (2021) zebrafish tailbud active fluid-to-solid jamming transition & yield-stress axis elongation — Parameter expressivity: 91/100" ;
