    dct:description "All 5 Mongera/Lawton regimes (`evaluate_all_perturbation_regimes`, L920-973) plus 3 new Dray fibronectin regimes (`evaluate_fibronectin_regimes`, L808-855) are evaluated; the 12-point fn_scale sweep (`sweep_fibronectin_scale`, L858-878) is monotonic in both elongation speed (increasing) and tailbud width (decreasing), asserted in self-test check 9 and shown in Panel C5; the clock period and fn_scale are exposed as CLI flags (L1987-1988) alongside the Pass 2 flags, and somite length scales with wavefront speed across regimes (Panel C3/C5). Deductions: the fn_scale sweep saturates above ~0.6 so the WT point sits on a flat shoulder, which limits the diagnostic value of the sweep near WT (-4); Lambda_arrest, c_slow, K_FN and K_t are not swept, and no 2D sweep (fn_scale x phi_ECS) is shown (-5)." ;
